% Checked examples of the composition/extraction fragment; no arithmetic solver.
cmr98_examples: THEORY
BEGIN
 IMPORTING cmr98_bv
 x,y,z: VAR bvec[8]
 a,b: VAR bvec[4]
 identity: THEOREM (x^(7,4) o x^(3,0))=x
 nested: THEOREM (x^(6,1))^(4,2)=x^(5,3)
 shared: THEOREM x=y AND y=z IMPLIES x=z
 crossing: THEOREM (a o b)^(5,2) = a^(1,0) o b^(3,2)
 propagate: THEOREM x^(7,4)=a AND a=b IMPLIES x^(7,4)=b
 overlap: THEOREM x^(7,1)=x^(6,0) IMPLIES x^(7,7)=x^(0,0)
 conflict: THEOREM x^(7,4)=bvec0[4] AND x^(5,2)=bvec1[4] IMPLIES FALSE
 multi: THEOREM x=(a o b) AND y=(b o a) IMPLIES x^(7,4)=y^(3,0)
 constants: THEOREM (bvec0[4] o bvec0[4])=bvec0[8]
 wide: THEOREM FORALL (v,w: bvec[1000000]): v=w IMPLIES v^(999999,500000)=w^(999999,500000)
 % Deliberate non-theorems: regression guards must leave these unproved.
 false_equality: CONJECTURE x=y
 false_overlap: CONJECTURE x^(7,2)=x^(5,0) IMPLIES x^(7,7)=x^(0,0)
END cmr98_examples
